+# Bug Fix: Preserve orders after customer deletion and fix admin pagination
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T21:58:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+The private customer-order endpoint now queries retained order customer ids without requiring the customer account to exist, while existing customers are still populated on returned orders. Admin order pagination now preserves totals for empty/out-of-range pages, calculates page counts with ceiling division, and groups name/phone OR predicates so filters remain scoped correctly.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` | modified | Customer order listing uses `OrderCriteria.customerId`; deleted customers no longer cause 404 and returned customer is nullable. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java` | modified | Corrected filter grouping and initialized count/page metadata and empty order lists. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java` | modified | Corrected total-pages calculation to ceiling division. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Empty pages retain matching `recordsTotal` and `totalPages`. |
+| `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/business/utils/RepositoryHelperTest.java` | added test | Pins down zero-based page offsets and ceiling page totals. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- `com.salesmanager.test.business.utils.RepositoryHelperTest#usesZeroBasedPagesAndCeilingTotalPages` — verifies page 1 starts at offset 10 for page size 10 and 21 records reports 3 pages.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed; all six reactor modules compiled successfully.
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=RepositoryHelperTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed; 1 test, 0 failures.
+- Manual checks: reviewed the private customer-order route, detail mapping, repository filters, and empty-page response path.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The assessment identified the existing nullable detail mapping as already compatible with deleted customers, so no change was required to the detail endpoint or order persistence model. The requested customer-id behavior was implemented through the existing facade/service path rather than adding a new service method.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add a database-backed order API integration fixture covering deletion, re-registration, historical detail, payment/history, and filtered admin pages when the project’s integration environment is available.
